+# Grouped device-resident E2 dispatch: rejected operator prototype
+
+Date: 2026-09-03
+
+## Verdict
+
+Reject before full model load. A compact GPU job planner and persistent E2
+workers preserved the accepted large-row trellis math and removed the CPU count
+read plus Python expert loop. At the exact 288-expert GLM dimensions, however,
+the complete MoE layer was neutral at 2,048 rows and 1.6-1.7% slower at the
+other production shapes.
+
+The prototype runtime and extension code were removed. The accepted paired and
+fused per-expert E2 path remains the default.
+
+## Design
+
+One GPU planning block converted the 288 routing counts into compact
+`(expert, row tile, output tile)` jobs. The candidate then executed:
+
+1. compact gather plus input SUH/Hadamard for fat routes;
+2. persistent grouped paired gate/up E2 jobs;
+3. grouped bit-exact SwiGLU plus down-input SUH/Hadamard;
+4. persistent grouped down E2 jobs with atomic weighted scatter.
+
+Thin experts still ran through the unchanged stock persistent MoE kernel. Fat
+scratch was bounded by the number of routed assignments and reused between
+layers.
+
+The first build exposed an indexing error because ExLlamaV3's inherited
+Hadamard primitive uses `blockIdx.y` internally for scale addressing. Moving
+expert identity to grid-Z fixed it: single-route outputs then became bit-exact,
+and top-8 results differed only by atomic accumulation order.
+
+## Exact-shape result
+
+One idle GB10, K4 MCG, hidden width 4,096, TP-local intermediate width 1,024,
+288 experts, top-8 distinct Zipf-skewed routing, two warmups and three measured
+iterations. Timing covers the complete routed-expert apply boundary, including
+sorting, count creation, thin and fat execution, activation, scatter, host
+synchronization, and launch gaps.
+
+| Tokens | Fat experts | Maximum expert rows | Accepted E2 (ms) | Grouped E2 (ms) | Candidate / accepted |
+| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 512 | 5 | 403 | 11.873 | 12.071 | 0.984x |
+| 2,048 | 22 | 1,597 | 23.014 | 22.985 | 1.001x |
+| 7,168 | 82 | 5,524 | 59.420 | 60.472 | 0.983x |
+
+All outputs were finite. Maximum absolute difference was 4.0 in FP16-returned
+outputs whose maximum magnitude was about 20-23K, or 0.017-0.021% relative.
+Mean absolute difference was approximately 0.000014-0.000023.
+
+## Interpretation
+
+The accepted path already copies counts on a side stream while thin experts
+run. Consequently, the visible CPU synchronization and Python loop are not the
+dominant wall term once the paired/fused E2 kernels are active. The grouped
+candidate trades those costs for compact-route traffic, job planning, and
+atomic scatter, yielding no net production-shape gain.
+
+Do not spend another full-model iteration on MoE dispatch without a profile
+showing that this balance changed. The next large-lever work should move to the
+sparse prefill/KDA/TP2 terms and retain the accepted E2 pipeline.
